{#-
  base-task.jinja2 — the shared spine every lmer taskdef extends.

  A taskdef body contains only what makes it that task: it
  `{% extends 'base-task.jinja2' %}` and overrides the blocks below.
  Every block is individually overridable; `task_phases` is the required
  per-task middle — a body that does not override it renders an empty
  work section, so always provide it.

  Block interface (ordered as rendered):
    intro            — REQUIRED: H1 title + what the task is
    service_mode     — service-mode partial (rarely overridden)
    run_state        — durable run-state contract (rarely overridden)
    branch_setup     — Phase -1 branch rules; suppress for read-only tasks
    self_dev         — self-development mode rules (conditional partial)
    phase0_tools     — Phase 0 tool orientation; contains provider_tooling
    provider_tooling — nested: provider CLI guidance (github/gitlab)
    project_info     — the mandatory `work read-project-info` contract
    secrets          — secrets-in-logs policy (extend with `{{ super() }}`)
    clean_gate       — Phase 0.5 clean-state gate-check
    task_phases      — REQUIRED: the task's own phases/workflow
    changelog        — changelog maintenance partial
    phasic           — phasic work-mode partial
    delivery         — After Pushing: MR/PR creation
    close_out        — closing out the run
    do_not           — the DO-NOT list; add rules via nested do_not_extra
    do_not_extra     — nested: task-specific DO-NOT additions

  Renaming or removing a block here is a schema bump (Jinja silently drops
  child blocks whose name no longer exists in the parent) — see
  docs/TASKDEFS.md, "Block-interface stability policy".
-#}
