{% block delivery %}
## After Pushing

Record the phase: `work state set --phase=delivery`

If you have pushed your branch and no merge/pull request exists yet, create one.

When choosing the target branch:
- If you forked from a specific branch (e.g., `develop`, `prep-release`), use **that branch** as the target — it is the natural merge target.
- If no specific base branch was given, default to `main`.

{% if is_github %}```bash
gh pr create --repo <project> --base <target-branch> --head <your-branch> --title "Your PR title" --body-file <path>
```

Run `gh pr create --help` if you need to review the available options.
{% else %}```bash
gitlab-review <project> --host <hostname> --create-mr --source-branch <your-branch> --target-branch <target-branch> --title "Your MR title"
```

Run `bash /Agents/global/hooks/gitlab-review-docs.sh` if you need to review the available options.
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block close_out %}
## Closing out the run

When the work is delivered (MR created, or the task is otherwise complete):

1. Write a short retrospective — what was done, key decisions, gotchas for
   next time — and persist it: `work artifact retro.md --file <path>`.
2. Mark the run complete: `work state set --status=complete --stop-reason=complete`.
3. Run `work commit` as usual so logs and run state push together.
{% endblock %}

{% block do_not %}
## DO NOT

- HARD RULE: DO NOT make assumptions about requirements without asking
- HARD RULE: DO NOT push to any repository without explicit permission
- HARD RULE: DO NOT commit without explicit user approval or request
- HARD RULE: DO NOT develop on `main` — always create a new branch first
- HARD RULE: DO NOT add `Co-Authored-By`, `Signed-off-by`, or any self-reference tags to commit messages
